      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017. Published by Elsevier Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "Infective endocarditis (IE) after transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI) is a rare but severe complication. Among 326 patients who underwent TAVI in Grenoble Alpes university hospital, 6 (1.8%) IE cases and 11 (3.4%) bacteraemia cases were identified. No EI was linked to the intervention; one was due to Staphylococcus aureus despite a screening and targeted decolonization strategy. This underscores the need for randomized studies to evaluate benefit and cost-effectiveness of this policy."
      },
